# --- environments and build output -----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- machine-specific infrastructure state ---------------------------------
# Both are GENERATED by scripts/ and describe one particular deployment: VPC and
# subnet ids, endpoint hostnames, instance ids, the Elastic IP. None of it is
# secret, but none of it is source either - committing it means the next person
# to run the scripts gets a merge conflict describing someone else's account.
# config/env.sh is committed and holds the defaults; these hold the results.
config/env.local.sh
config/env.local.sh.tmp.*
.deploy-state.json
# The AgentCore Gateway spike's live pointers: gateway id/url, Cedar policy-engine
# id, role ARN, for one particular account. Generated by the gateway scripts, not
# source - same reasoning as .deploy-state.json.
.gateway-spike.json

# --- credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. Salesforce credentials are read from AWS Secrets Manager
# (hvi/salesforce) and SF_CLIENT_ID / SF_CLIENT_SECRET are deliberately empty in
# config/env.sh, so nothing here should ever hold a secret. These patterns exist
# so that a future shortcut - pasting a key into a local override to debug
# something at 2am - cannot become a commit.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
**/secrets.json
**/credentials.json

# --- third-party documents --------------------------------------------------
# Insurer proposal forms, used as the SOURCE for the form schema. They are
# copyrighted by their publishers and are not ours to redistribute. The useful
# artifact is the extracted, structured result, and seed/form-*.json IS committed
# so the schema's provenance is still legible without republishing the PDFs.
seed/source/*.pdf

# --- binary documents and images -------------------------------------------
# Office documents and screenshots are not part of the codebase.
*.docx
*.pptx
*.png

# --- model weight artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# The OmniVoice SageMaker inference SOURCE under models/*/code/ is committed; the
# downloaded/built model weights and packaged tarballs are not (they are large,
# regenerable, and in OmniVoice's case CC-BY-NC licensed).
models/**/*.tar.gz
models/**/*.bin
models/**/*.safetensors
models/**/*.pt
models/**/*.onnx

# --- local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log
/tmp/
echo-in.wav
echo-out.wav
*.swp
# Auto-generated code-review artifacts and one-off forensic scripts. Tool output
# and 2am debugging, never part of the suite - tests/tmp_*.py are scratch, the
# committed suites are tests/test_*.py.
semantic-review/
tests/tmp_*.py
